+/*
+ * The speaker stream iOS plays into (userland/audio/audio_plugin.c writes 48 kHz 16-bit stereo frames
+ * to /dev/redwood-audio = /dev/topaz-audio). Legacy ASM pushes buffers: a 1 s ring is mapped once
+ * (SID 1 through the identity bank above), and while playing the audio thread hands it to the ADSP in
+ * 20 ms chunks (ASM_DATA_CMD_WRITE_V2), four in flight, the next one on each write-done. write() puts
+ * frames 40 ms ahead of what was handed over and zeroes the ring behind the data, so nothing old
+ * replays. The session runs when frames come and pauses 0.5 s after the last one; the TAS2557 is
+ * powered with it (Linux tas2557 startup / shutdown data), so the idle phone pays for neither.
+ * Volume: iOS's (eighths of a dB under the loudest, or muted) scales the samples as they are copied.
+ * Verified first with a 1 kHz tone (2026-11-24): 34 buffers of 100 ms played, the laptop mic heard it.
+ */
